<title>PAKISTAN: Karachi port handles 68,490 tonnes cargo.</title>
<headline>Karachi port handles 68,490 tonnes cargo.</headline>
<dateline>KARACHI, Pakistan 1996-09-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Pakistan's Karachi Port Trust said it had handled 68,490 tonnes of export and import cargo in 24 hours to 7.00 a.m. (0200 GMT) on Thursday compared to 78,263 tonnes in the same period on Wednesday.</p>
<p>Cargo handling in tonnes:</p>
<p>						Wednesday   Sept 18</p>
<p>    Export cargo			   7,721     10,784</p>
<p>    Import cargo			  60,769     67,479</p>
<p>In the past 24 hours, six ships sailed and seven berthed. In the next 24 hours, four were expected to sail and eight were expected to arrive.  </p>
<p>Berthing schedule of major vessels unloading or expected to unload at Karachi Port:</p>
<p>    Commodity	  Tonnes/TEUs  Ship		   Berthing</p>
<p>Gas oil		  56,000	 Keefan		 19/9</p>
<p>Palm oil		 10,800	 Tiblisi		19/9</p>
<p>Palm oil		  8,000	 Strength	     21/9</p>
<p>Gas oil		  40,000	 Santa Lucia	  21/9</p>
<p>Crude oil		61,000	 Capitan Miranda    21/9</p>
<p>Palm oil		 13,000	 Bunga Anggarik     23/9</p>
<p>-- Karachi newsroom 9221-5685192</p>
